<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis H1 sales rise 19 pct.</title>
<headline>Novartis H1 sales rise 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30.</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group sales		    16,562	    vs 13,891</p>
<p>Note - Full name of Swiss life sciences group is Novartis AG. Group sales were 19 percent higher on a Swiss franc basis and seven percent higher in local currencies.  </p>
<p>Sales by Division</p>
<p>    HEALTHCARE		  9,193	     vs 7,599</p>
<p> Pharmaceuticals		6,928	     vs 5,648</p>
<p> Consumer Health		829		 vs 780</p>
<p> Generics			 738		 vs 595</p>
<p> CIBA Vision		    698		 vs 576</p>
<p>    AGRIBUSINESS		5,285	     vs 4,548</p>
<p> Crop Protection		3,758	     vs 3,218</p>
<p> Seeds			    1,029	     vs 838</p>
<p> Animal Health		  498		 vs 492</p>
<p>    NUTRITION		   2,084	     vs 1,744</p>
<p>    TOTAL			 16,562	    vs 13,891</p>
<p>Note - Novartis was formed through the merger of Sandoz AG and Ciba-Geigy AG at the end of 1996. Novartis said it introduced a new uniform net sales definition and for comparability, the corresponding 1996 figures have been redefined accordingly. Figures also exclude divested activities. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
